<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Geoffrey Plantagenet, Count of Anjou</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1113–1151</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Geoffrey V of Anjou, Geoffrey Plantagenet</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Geoffrey Plantagenet, Count of Anjou, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/touraine">Touraine</a> and Maine, married Matilda, daughter of Henry I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, in 1128. He conquered Normandy in the 1140s while Matilda fought Stephen for the English throne. Their son Henry II joined Anjou, Normandy, England and Aquitaine into the Angevin Empire, and the Plantagenet name derives from Geoffrey.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/geoffrey-plantagenet-count-of-anjou.jpg" alt="Geoffrey Plantagenet, Count of Anjou" width="320" height="611" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original creater of enamel unknown. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Geoffrey_of_Anjou_Monument.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
